<!--Post: 9030--><!--Time: 1109384591-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9030"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 6:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The man in custody is not Norman Williams.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9030-->
<!--Post: 9039--><!--Time: 1109385427-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9039"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lmuncy316<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lmuncy316<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 6:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Read the poem entitled &#34;Confused&#34; by Norman Williams on poetry.com <BR> <BR>I would copy and paste the poems but I believe Tom would not allow that. <BR> <BR>Also, does anybody know if the Norman Williams in custody has a middle name were even initial? <BR> <BR>In btk&#39;s letter &#40;the first one I think, check to make sure&#41; expresses his feelings that he cannot control the person within himself who commits the murders.  He says the monster inside himself decides who did victims will be and he cannot stop him. <BR> <BR>The poem acknowledges that the writer is confused with what he knows his right and with what his inner monster inevitably does.  Just when he thinks he can control the monster in his head another special person is provided for him.  And no matter how much he would like for it to end he knows it will not end. <BR> <BR>Emergency -- Larry King just said he will discuss BTK with John Walsh<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9039-->
<!--Post: 9043--><!--Time: 1109386391-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9043"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 6:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lmuncy316, are you paying attention to the world around you?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9043-->
