<!--Post: 9054--><!--Time: 1109387985-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9054"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lmuncy316<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lmuncy316<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 7:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno, if the man&#39;s name isn&#39;t Norman Williams.  Then so be it!  I was going well what I learned on the media thread. <BR> <BR>And, since you know it&#39;s not Norman Williams, do you know, or would you mind sharing the name of the person taken into custody?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9054-->
<!--Post: 9055--><!--Time: 1109388243-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9055"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 7:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s believed to be Dennis Lynn Rader, a Park City Compliance Director with the city.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9055-->
<!--Post: 9058--><!--Time: 1109389555-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9058"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lmuncy316<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lmuncy316<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 7:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno, other people are also saying his name is Jason Henry!  I&#39;m not saying it&#39;s not Dennis Lynn Rader, but who or what was your source of information?  If your source is reliable then I tip my hat to you!  However, if your source is no more reliable than mine you have no right to assume I&#39;m wrong and you&#39;re right.  I&#39;m not even saying I&#39;m right.  In fact, one thing makes me question how it could be Norman Williams.  The media is saying, at this moment, that they are waiting on DNA results.  I have heard that they may get the results anywhere from six to eight hours from now.  I have also heard they will not get the results until Tuesday!  The reason why this makes me doubt that it may be Norman Williams is the fact that Norman, according to what I have read, gave a DNA sample well over a month ago.  So, why would they need to wait for DNA results if it was him?  If it was Norman they should have gotten the results a long time ago.  And with the same flip of the coin, if DNA results matched BTK to Norman over a month ago &#40;or maybe not that long ago&#41; that would have given the Police Department, FBI, Mayor, Congressman, SWAT team, and other law authorities to plan a well orchestrated blitz like the one that was performed today.  If nothing else, read the poem for fun and reread btk&#39;s letters.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9058-->
